  "question": {
    "text": "The hydrocarbon which can react with sodium in liquid ammonia is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Jg34j",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{C} \\equiv \\mathrm{CCH}_2 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{CH}_3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "yPb9k",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{C} \\equiv \\mathrm{CH}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "85LRP",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{CH}=\\mathrm{CHCH}_3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "USorI",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{C} \\equiv \\mathrm{CCH}_2 \\mathrm{CH}_3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{CH}_2-\\mathrm{C} \\equiv \\mathrm{CH} \\stackrel{\\mathrm{Na} / \\mathrm{Liq} 9 \\mathrm{NH}}{\\Delta} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{C} \\equiv \\stackrel{\\ominus}{\\mathrm{C}} \\mathrm{Na}^{\\oplus}\n$$\nIt is a terminal alkyne, having acidic hydrogen.\nNote: Solve it as a case of terminal alkynes, otherwise all alkynes react with $\\mathrm{Na}$ in liq. $\\mathrm{NH}_3$.",
